{"id": "De1p6BYxw4E", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Ram once fired a BRAHMASTRA at a crow. With a blade of grass 🌱 The Crow and the Grass | Ramayan Part 4 of 12\n\n🏞️ In the forest of Chitrakoot, Ram and Sita rested by the water. A crow kept pecking at Sita. She threw a clod of earth. It came back, and clawed her until she bled. (Sundara Kanda 38)\n👑 Ram woke and saw the blood. This was no ordinary crow. It was Indra's own son.\n🌱 Ram picked up a blade of grass, and turned it into a Brahmastra.\n🌍 The crow fled through all three worlds. His father Indra, the gods, the sages: no one would shelter him. So he came back, and fell at Ram's feet.\n👁️ A Brahmastra can never be wasted. So the crow gave up his right eye, and Ram spared him.\n💔 Years later, in Lanka, Sita told Hanuman this story, a secret only Ram would know. And she asked: for a crow, a Brahmastra. Why not for the demon who took me?\n\n➡️ Part 5: one man against FOURTEEN THOUSAND demons. Follow @therishikatha so you don't miss it!\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. Insta Family Sale on Books 1–3, till 25 Oct → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 Comment JAI SHRI RAM if you're watching the whole series 🙏\n🔖 Save this, and share it with someone who loves the Ramayan\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #jayanta #brahmastra #sita #shriram #valmikiramayana #jaishriram #sanatandharma #hindumythology #indianmythology #ramayanseries #kidsbooks #rishikatha #mythologyforkids", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792761875, "like_count": 3904, "comment_count": 34, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1425953989004631a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 54.857, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQN5WZbit1JJo_Et